WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:17.810
A lower G.I.

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:25.270
endoscopy, also called colonoscopy or sigmoidoscopy,
allows your doctor to view the mucosal lining

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:29.120
of your lower gastrointestinal tract.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:33.910
The procedure is used as a screening test
in individuals with no symptoms or to help

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:38.870
diagnose unexplained abdominal pain, rectal
bleeding, or a change in bowel habits.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:50.660
It is capable of detecting inflammation, infections,
ulcers, diverticulosis, intestinal narrowing,

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:59.059
colorectal polyps, cancer, or other problems
that may be present.

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:03.809
Before the procedure you will need to undergo
bowel preparation.

00:01:03.809 --> 00:01:09.020
Depending on the type of medication prescribed
to you, you will start 1 to 3 days before

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:11.759
the procedure.

00:01:11.759 --> 00:01:16.100
You will need to modify your diet as well
as take medication, which will help to clear

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:20.310
your bowels in preparation for the procedure.

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:25.840
The procedure is performed using an endoscope,
which is a long, thin, flexible tube with

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:29.860
a light and a tiny video camera attached to
the end.

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:34.369
The camera transmits an image to a monitor.

00:01:34.369 --> 00:01:41.170
In a sigmoidoscopy the endoscope only reaches
to the top of the descending colon.

00:01:41.170 --> 00:01:46.020
In a colonoscopy the endoscope reaches through
the entire length of the colon, to where it

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:51.250
connects to the small intestine.

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:56.840
The presence of the endoscope and the air
may cause you to feel cramping or pressure

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:58.240
and the need to pass gas.

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:02.610
This is considered a normal part of the procedure.

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:07.079
Your doctor may ask you to change your position
slightly to help maneuver the endoscope more

00:02:07.079 --> 00:02:10.259
easily through the curves of your lower intestine.

00:02:10.259 --> 00:02:15.370
If you experience pain, tell your doctor immediately.

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:21.000
In some cases, your doctor may find it necessary
to take a biopsy.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:26.450
A biopsy helps distinguish between benign
and cancerous tissues and can help determine

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:31.140
the cause of bleeding, inflammation, or diarrhea.

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:36.310
Biopsies are often taken, even when your doctor
does not suspect cancer.

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:41.020
If one or more polyps are discovered, your
doctor will generally remove them in a procedure

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:43.760
called a polypectomy.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:50.280
He or she will usually use a snare to remove
the polyps and then cauterize their bases

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:52.870
to control bleeding.

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:59.530
At the end of your procedure the endoscope
will be removed from your colon.

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:05.930
A sigmoidoscopy usually takes about twenty
minutes, while a colonoscopy can take thirty

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:07.109
minutes to an hour.

